-- CODEX INSURANCE LIMITED -- Hospital Income Benefit Policy
-- L4 encoding: fact schema (verbatim from schema.md) plus the `covered`
-- predicate, which is TRUE exactly when a benefit is payable on the claim.

IMPORT prelude

DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF Sickness, `Accidental injury`, Neither

DECLARE Cause IS ONE OF
  Skydiving, `Military service`, Firefighting, `Police service`, Other

DECLARE Claim
  HAS `agreement signed`                           IS A BOOLEAN
      `premium paid month`                         IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `hospitalization month`                      IS A NUMBER
      `hospitalization ground`                     IS A Ground
      `age at hospitalization`                     IS A NUMBER
      `causes`                                     IS A LIST OF Cause
      `fraud month`                                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `misrepresentation month`                    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit month`                       IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit provider qualified`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `written confirmation month`                 IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `dispute arisen`                             IS A BOOLEAN
      `unable to settle month`                     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `arbitration commenced month`                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `valid arbitration award issued`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `written proof of claim month`               IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `recovery sought month`                      IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `policy term months`                         IS A NUMBER
      `confined in us hospital`                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `continuous confinement days`                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `claim made setting out basis`               IS A BOOLEAN

-- Supporting helpers (pre-defined -- call them, do not redefine them)

GIVEN  `event month` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
       `limit month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no later than` MEANS
  CONSIDER `event month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST m  THEN m AT MOST `limit month`

GIVEN  cs IS A LIST OF Cause
       c  IS A Cause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arose out of` MEANS elem c cs

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `Section 1 -- Policy in Effect and Conditions`
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§ `1.1 The policy is in effect`
-- The policy is in effect if the agreement is signed, the premium has been
-- paid (due, per section 4.5, at the signing of the policy, i.e. no later
-- than month 0), and the policy has not been canceled.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the policy is in effect` claim MEANS
        (claim's `agreement signed`)
    AND `no later than` (claim's `premium paid month`) 0
    AND NOT (`the policy has been canceled` claim)

§§ `1.2 Cancelation`
-- Cancelation is deemed to occur on fraud, on misrepresentation or material
-- withholding of information, on failure to satisfy the section 1.3
-- condition in a timely fashion, or automatically once the policy term has
-- run out.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the policy has been canceled` claim MEANS
        isJust (claim's `fraud month`)
    OR  isJust (claim's `misrepresentation month`)
    OR  NOT (`the wellness visit condition has been satisfied` claim)
    OR  (claim's `hospitalization month`) GREATER THAN (claim's `policy term months`)

§§ `1.3 Wellness visit and written confirmation`
-- No later than the 7th month anniversary of the effective date, written
-- confirmation must be supplied of a wellness visit, with a qualified
-- medical provider, occurring no later than the 6th month anniversary.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the wellness visit condition has been satisfied` claim MEANS
        `no later than` (claim's `wellness visit month`) 6
    AND (claim's `wellness visit provider qualified`)
    AND `no later than` (claim's `written confirmation month`) 7

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `Section 2 -- Benefits`
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§ `2.1 Ground for hospitalization`
-- A benefit is payable only for hospitalization as a result of sickness or
-- accidental injury -- not for a hospitalization on neither ground.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the hospitalization ground is covered` claim MEANS
  CONSIDER (claim's `hospitalization ground`)
    WHEN Sickness            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Accidental injury` THEN TRUE
    WHEN Neither             THEN FALSE

§§ `2.2 Continuous confinement in a United States hospital`
-- The benefit is only payable for continuous confinement in a hospital in
-- the United States, for a period not exceeding 365 days.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the continuous confinement conditions are met` claim MEANS
        (claim's `confined in us hospital`)
    AND `no later than` (claim's `continuous confinement days`) 365

-- 2.3 "a claim must be made ... setting out the basis for making the claim"
-- is the Claim's own `claim made setting out basis` field, used directly in
-- `covered` below; no separate helper is needed for it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `Section 3 -- General Exclusions`
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- No benefit is payable where the sickness or accidental injury arose
-- directly or indirectly out of skydiving, service in the military,
-- service as a firefighter, or service in the police, or where the
-- claimant's age at the time of hospitalization is 80 or more.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a general exclusion applies` claim MEANS
        `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) Skydiving
    OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) `Military service`
    OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) Firefighting
    OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) `Police service`
    OR  (claim's `age at hospitalization`) AT LEAST 80

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `Section 4 -- General Conditions`
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§ `4.2 Arbitration`
-- If a dispute or disagreement has arisen, arbitration must be commenced
-- within three months of the parties becoming unable to settle, and the
-- issuance of a valid arbitration award is a condition precedent to
-- liability. Independently of any dispute, "in no case" may recovery be
-- sought within sixty days of written proof of claim being submitted --
-- taken here as two months, since this schema only tracks month-level
-- granularity elsewhere.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arbitration was commenced in time` claim MEANS
  CONSIDER (claim's `unable to settle month`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST m  THEN `no later than` (claim's `arbitration commenced month`) (m PLUS 3)

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the arbitration conditions are satisfied` claim MEANS
    NOT (claim's `dispute arisen`)
    OR  (    `arbitration was commenced in time` claim
         AND (claim's `valid arbitration award issued`))

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`recovery was not sought prematurely` claim MEANS
  CONSIDER (claim's `written proof of claim month`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST wpc THEN
      CONSIDER (claim's `recovery sought month`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST rs THEN rs AT LEAST (wpc PLUS 2)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `covered`
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- A benefit is payable on the claim exactly when: the policy is in effect;
-- the hospitalization is on a covered ground; the continuous-confinement
-- conditions are met; a proper claim has been made; no section 3 general
-- exclusion applies; and the section 4.2 arbitration/recovery-timing
-- conditions are satisfied.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
covered claim MEANS
        `the policy is in effect` claim
    AND `the hospitalization ground is covered` claim
    AND `the continuous confinement conditions are met` claim
    AND (claim's `claim made setting out basis`)
    AND NOT (`a general exclusion applies` claim)
    AND `the arbitration conditions are satisfied` claim
    AND `recovery was not sought prematurely` claim
